# 2. Non-negotiable design principles

## 2.1 UE is the source of truth

The authoritative UI contract lives in Unreal through reflected properties, reflected types, metadata, and delegates/events.

The generated schema and TypeScript files are output artifacts.

Developers should not manually maintain a duplicate frontend schema unless they explicitly opt into an override.

```text
UE reflection
  -> infer state keys
  -> infer JS/TS types
  -> infer enum values
  -> infer numeric ranges
  -> infer event payloads
  -> generate schema JSON
  -> generate TypeScript facade
  -> generate preview controls
  -> drive runtime bridge
```

## 2.2 Normal user code should not use raw string matching

This is not acceptable as the happy path:

```ts
ui.on("PlayerFiredShot", payload => {});
ui.bindStyle("#crosshair", "--spread", "currentSpread", v => `${v}px`);
```

That API may exist internally or as a low-level escape hatch, but normal frontend code should use a generated facade:

```ts
const hud = createMainHUD();

hud.state.currentSpread.bindStyle("#crosshair", "--spread", v => `${v}px`);

hud.state.crosshairMode.bindClass("#crosshair", mode => `crosshair ${mode}`);

hud.events.PlayerFiredShot.on(({ gunType, ammoRemaining, spread }) => {
  playCrosshairKick(gunType, spread);
});
```

The user should get autocomplete for:

```ts
hud.state.currentSpread
hud.state.crosshairMode
hud.events.PlayerFiredShot
hud.events.HitConfirmed
```

If a UE property or delegate is renamed or removed, generated TypeScript should change and frontend compile errors should reveal the mismatch.

## 2.3 State and events are separate

Persistent state and one-shot events must not be mixed.

| Concept | Meaning            | Examples                                                 |
| ------- | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| State   | Current UI state   | health, ammo, spread, interaction prompt, crosshair mode |
| Event   | Something happened | PlayerFiredShot, HitConfirmed, TookDamage, ReloadStarted |

State is dirty-checked and patched.

Events are emitted when they occur.

## 2.4 The frontend handles presentation, not game glue

The web side should handle:

```text
layout
styling
animation
DOM/CSS updates
visual reactions to typed events
```

The web side should not handle:

```text
figuring out what UE properties exist
manually matching raw event strings
manual JSON parsing
manual dirty checking
manual schema maintenance
manual bridge setup
```

## 2.5 The dynamic HUD sample is dogfooding

The dynamic crosshair sample must be built using the exact public generated API intended for users.

No special crosshair-specific API should be used initially.

The sample should prove:

```text
property inference works
enum inference works
event inference works
preview controls work
generated TS facade is pleasant
no raw strings needed in normal frontend code
same HUD code works in preview and UE runtime
```

