# 6. Automatic property inference

## 6.1 Supported state types

Initial required support:

| UE type                         | TypeScript type        | Preview control                     |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `bool`                          | `boolean`              | checkbox                            |
| `int32`, `int64`, `uint8`, etc. | `number`               | slider + number input               |
| `float`, `double`               | `number`               | slider + number input               |
| `FString`                       | `string`               | text input                          |
| `FName`                         | `string`               | text input or dropdown if enum-like |
| `FText`                         | `string`               | text input                          |
| `UENUM` / enum byte             | string union preferred | dropdown                            |

Later support should include:

```text
FVector2D
FVector
FLinearColor
FGameplayTag
FGameplayTagContainer
simple USTRUCT payloads
arrays/lists
object references by display name/id
```

## 6.2 Property reader

Use Unreal reflection:

```cpp
FProperty* Property = SourceObject->GetClass()->FindPropertyByName(PropertyName);
```

Then use `CastField`:

```cpp
FBoolProperty
FNumericProperty
FStrProperty
FNameProperty
FTextProperty
FEnumProperty
FByteProperty
FStructProperty
FArrayProperty
```

All values must be converted to a JS-compatible JSON value.

Example mapping:

```cpp
bool          -> true / false
int32         -> number
float         -> number
FString       -> string
FName         -> string
FText         -> string
enum          -> string name, not raw number, unless configured otherwise
```

Enums should default to generated string unions:

```ts
crosshairMode: "Default" | "Combat" | "Interact";
```

