# 7. Automatic range/control inference

The preview system must infer controls from reflection metadata.

## 7.1 Metadata to read

For numeric properties, inspect metadata such as:

```cpp
ClampMin
ClampMax
UIMin
UIMax
Delta
Multiple
SliderExponent
Units
```

Example:

```cpp
UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere, BlueprintReadWrite, meta=(ClampMin="0", ClampMax="100", UIMin="0", UIMax="100"))
float Health;
```

Generated preview schema:

```json
{
  "health": {
    "type": "number",
    "min": 0,
    "max": 100,
    "step": 1,
    "default": 100
  }
}
```

## 7.2 Preview defaults

If metadata is missing, use safe heuristics.

| Property hint                       | Default              |
| ----------------------------------- | -------------------- |
| health, stamina, energy             | `0..100`, step `1`   |
| percent, alpha, opacity, normalized | `0..1`, step `0.01`  |
| spread, recoil                      | `0..40`, step `0.1`  |
| ammo, count, charges                | `0..100`, step `1`   |
| generic float                       | `0..100`, step `0.1` |
| generic int                         | `0..100`, step `1`   |
| bool                                | checkbox             |
| enum                                | dropdown             |
| string/text                         | text input           |

Metadata always overrides heuristics.

## 7.3 Overrides

The binding asset should allow optional overrides:

```text
web-facing field name
default preview value
min/max/step
enum display labels
update rate
float tolerance
hidden from preview
read-only in preview
```

But these are overrides, not the normal contract source.

