# 8. Automatic event inference

## 8.1 Event sources

Support at least:

```text
BlueprintAssignable dynamic multicast delegates
C++ dynamic multicast delegates
explicit manual Emit calls
```

The normal final UX should be picker-driven:

```text
Source: Weapon
Event: OnPlayerFiredShot
Web event name: PlayerFiredShot, auto-suggested
Payload: inferred from delegate params
```

## 8.2 Delegate payload inference

Example C++ delegate:

```cpp
DECLARE_DYNAMIC_MULTICAST_DELEGATE_ThreeParams(
    FOnPlayerFiredShot,
    FString, GunType,
    int32, AmmoRemaining,
    float, Spread
);

UPROPERTY(BlueprintAssignable)
FOnPlayerFiredShot OnPlayerFiredShot;
```

Generated TypeScript:

```ts
PlayerFiredShot: {
  gunType: string;
  ammoRemaining: number;
  spread: number;
};
```

The generator should normalize names:

```text
GunType -> gunType
AmmoRemaining -> ammoRemaining
Spread -> spread
```

Allow override if the generated names are wrong.

## 8.3 Event transport

At runtime, when a bound delegate fires:

```text
UE delegate fires
-> bridge receives params
-> converts params to JS-compatible payload
-> sends typed event to JS runtime
-> generated facade dispatches to hud.events.EventName
```

Events must not be treated as dirty state.

---

# 9. Dirty checking and batching

## 9.1 Runtime state patching

The runtime bridge should track last-sent values per binding.

Loop:

```text
for each bound state value:
  resolve source object
  read property
  convert to JSON value
  compare to last sent value
  if changed:
    add to patch
    update last sent value

if patch not empty:
  send one batched patch
```

Example patch:

```json
{
  "currentAmmo": 12,
  "currentSpread": 18.5,
  "crosshairMode": "Combat",
  "canInteract": true
}
```

## 9.2 Float tolerance

Float and double values should support tolerance to avoid noise:

```text
currentSpread tolerance: 0.05
health tolerance: 0.01
```

Default tolerance should be conservative.

## 9.3 Update rate

The bridge should support global and per-binding update rates.

Examples:

```text
currentSpread: 60 Hz
health: on change / 20 Hz
prompt: on change / 10 Hz
```

Implementation can start with tick polling plus rate limiting.

## 9.4 Initial sync

When the browser page reports ready:

```text
send full current state once
then resume dirty patches
```

The page-ready handshake is required. Do not send initial state before JS is ready.

