# 10. Generated TypeScript facade

This is central.

The generated TS facade is what prevents stringly typed frontend code.

## 10.1 Generated files

For `MainHUD`, generate:

```text
src/generated/MainHUD.generated.ts
src/generated/MainHUD.schema.json
src/generated/MainHUD.preview.json
```

The generated TS file is overwritten whenever the UE binding changes.

User-authored files must live outside `generated/`.

## 10.2 Generated facade example

```ts
// src/generated/MainHUD.generated.ts
// AUTO-GENERATED. DO NOT EDIT.

import {
  createGameWebUI,
  type GameWebUIRuntime,
  type StateField,
  type EventField,
} from "@gamewebui/client";

export type MainHUDState = {
  currentSpread: number;
  crosshairMode: "Default" | "Combat" | "Interact";
  canInteract: boolean;
  currentAmmo: number;
  prompt: string;
};

export type MainHUDEvents = {
  PlayerFiredShot: {
    gunType: string;
    ammoRemaining: number;
    spread: number;
  };

  HitConfirmed: void;

  TookDamage: {
    amount: number;
    direction: number;
  };
};

export type MainHUDRuntime = GameWebUIRuntime<MainHUDState, MainHUDEvents>;

export function createMainHUD(): MainHUDRuntime & {
  state: {
    currentSpread: StateField<MainHUDState, "currentSpread">;
    crosshairMode: StateField<MainHUDState, "crosshairMode">;
    canInteract: StateField<MainHUDState, "canInteract">;
    currentAmmo: StateField<MainHUDState, "currentAmmo">;
    prompt: StateField<MainHUDState, "prompt">;
  };

  events: {
    PlayerFiredShot: EventField<MainHUDEvents, "PlayerFiredShot">;
    HitConfirmed: EventField<MainHUDEvents, "HitConfirmed">;
    TookDamage: EventField<MainHUDEvents, "TookDamage">;
  };
} {
  const ui = createGameWebUI<MainHUDState, MainHUDEvents>({
    contractName: "MainHUD"
  });

  return ui.withFacade({
    stateKeys: {
      currentSpread: "currentSpread",
      crosshairMode: "crosshairMode",
      canInteract: "canInteract",
      currentAmmo: "currentAmmo",
      prompt: "prompt",
    },
    eventKeys: {
      PlayerFiredShot: "PlayerFiredShot",
      HitConfirmed: "HitConfirmed",
      TookDamage: "TookDamage",
    },
  }) as any;
}
```

The raw strings exist inside generated code only.

Normal user code uses properties and methods.

## 10.3 User frontend code example

```ts
import { createMainHUD } from "./generated/MainHUD.generated";

const hud = createMainHUD();

hud.state.currentSpread.bindStyle("#crosshair", "--spread", value => `${value}px`);

hud.state.crosshairMode.bindClass("#crosshair", mode => `crosshair ${mode}`);

hud.state.currentAmmo.bindText("#ammo", ammo => `${ammo}`);

hud.state.canInteract.bindVisible("#interaction-prompt");

hud.state.prompt.bindText("#interaction-prompt");

hud.events.PlayerFiredShot.on(({ gunType, ammoRemaining, spread }) => {
  playCrosshairKick(gunType, spread);
});

hud.events.HitConfirmed.on(() => {
  playHitmarker();
});

hud.ready();
```

No raw event string.
No raw state key string.
No manual patch inspection.

