# 12. JS client runtime

## 12.1 Generic internal client

The generated facade wraps a generic runtime.

The generic API may exist, but it is not the primary user-facing API.

Internal-ish primitives:

```ts
createGameWebUI<State, Events>()
ui.bindText(selector, key, mapper?)
ui.bindStyle(selector, property, key, mapper)
ui.bindClass(selector, key, mapper)
ui.bindVisible(selector, key, mapper?)
ui.watch(key, callback)
ui.on(eventName, callback)
ui.onPatch(callback)
ui.emitPreviewEvent(...)
ui.applyPreviewPatch(...)
```

Generated `StateField` methods should wrap those:

```ts
hud.state.currentSpread.bindStyle(...)
hud.state.currentAmmo.bindText(...)
hud.events.PlayerFiredShot.on(...)
```

## 12.2 Required generated field APIs

For state fields:

```ts
field.get(): T
field.watch(callback: (value: T) => void): Unsubscribe
field.bindText(selector, mapper?)
field.bindStyle(selector, cssProperty, mapper)
field.bindClass(selector, mapper)
field.bindAttr(selector, attrName, mapper)
field.bindVisible(selector?, mapper?)
```

For event fields:

```ts
event.on(callback): Unsubscribe
event.once(callback): Unsubscribe
```

For multi-field derived bindings, provide generated runtime helpers:

```ts
hud.derive(["health", "maxHealth"], ({ health, maxHealth }) => ...)
```

Or facade-friendly version:

```ts
hud.derive(
  [hud.state.health, hud.state.maxHealth],
  ({ health, maxHealth }) => ...
);
```

