# 17. Implementation completion criteria

The handover is considered complete only when the following are true:

## UE/editor side

```text
Binding asset can select reflected properties from dropdowns.
Binding asset can select reflected delegates/events from dropdowns.
Type inference works for bool/int/float/string/FName/FText/enums.
Range inference reads ClampMin/ClampMax/UIMin/UIMax.
Event payload inference works for selected dynamic multicast delegates.
Generated TS facade avoids raw string usage in normal frontend code.
Generated stubs are created once and not overwritten.
Runtime bridge dirty-checks and batches patches.
Runtime bridge forwards reflected events with payloads.
Initial sync happens after JS ready handshake.
Manual escape hatches exist but are not the primary path.
```

## JS side

```text
Generated facade exposes hud.state.field and hud.events.event.
State fields support bindText/bindStyle/bindClass/bindVisible/watch.
Event fields support on/once.
No raw string state/event names are needed in the dogfood sample.
Same frontend code works in runtime and preview.
```

## Preview side

```text
Dedicated preview window opens without UE running.
Preview controls are generated from UE-inferred schema.
Sliders/toggles/dropdowns update HUD live.
Event buttons trigger typed frontend event handlers.
Accurate preview uses the same CEF runtime as the BLUI backend where technically feasible.
```

## Dogfood sample

```text
Dynamic crosshair uses reflected UE values.
Crosshair spread updates from generated state facade.
Crosshair mode updates from generated enum facade.
Ammo text updates from generated state facade.
Interaction prompt visibility/text updates from generated state facade.
PlayerFiredShot event triggers visual recoil animation.
HitConfirmed event triggers hitmarker animation.
Preview can test all of the above without UE running.
```

