## Amendment 2: Preview window is a first-class tool, not an optional extra

The preview host should be treated as a core deliverable.

It must:

```text
- open as a dedicated standalone window
- use the same bundled CEF runtime as the selected backend
- load the generated HUD/web app
- load the generated schema
- generate controls from inferred UE metadata
- allow live slider/toggle/dropdown editing
- allow event buttons with inferred payload forms
- use the same generated TypeScript facade as runtime
```

The preview must be good enough that a frontend/UI developer can iterate on HUD styling and behavior without launching UE for every change.

---

## Amendment 3: Generated preview controls remain UE-reflection-driven

The preview control panel should not require a manually authored mock schema.

It is generated from Unreal reflection and metadata:

```text
UPROPERTY type
UPROPERTY name
UENUM values
ClampMin / ClampMax
UIMin / UIMax
BlueprintAssignable delegate params
optional binding overrides
```

So a property like:

```cpp
UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere, BlueprintReadWrite, meta=(ClampMin="0", ClampMax="40", UIMin="0", UIMax="40"))
float CurrentSpread;
```

generates:

```text
currentSpread
→ TypeScript: number
→ Preview control: slider 0..40
```

And a delegate like:

```cpp
OnPlayerFiredShot(FString GunType, int32 AmmoRemaining, float Spread)
```

generates:

```text
PlayerFiredShot event button
→ payload fields:
   gunType: text input
   ammoRemaining: number input
   spread: slider/number input
```

